3. Synthesis
3.1 Synthesis of Nonane-Based IAJDs with 3,5-Nonsymmetric Alkyl Chains 
Scheme S1. Synthesis of Nonane-Based IAJDs with 3,5-Nonsymmetric Alkyl Chains
Reagents and conditions: (i) K2CO3, KI, DMF, 80 °C, 5 h; (ii) RBr/ROTs, K2CO3, DMF, 120 °C, 2 h; 
(iii) H2, Pd/C, DCM, MeOH, 12 h; (iv) LiAlH4, THF, 0–23 °C, 1 h; (v) DCC, DPTS, DCM, 12 h; (vi) 
K2CO3, MeCN, 95 °C, 3 h.
Methyl 3-(benzyloxy)-5-(nonyloxy)benzoate (3). The synthesis of methyl 3-(benzyloxy)-5-
hydroxybenzoate (2) was adapted from literature procedures reported by our laboratory.
[3] A mixture of
compound 2 (6.50 g, 25.17 mmol, 1 equiv), 1-bromononane (5.74 g, 27.68 mmol, 1.1 equiv), K2CO3 (6.96
g, 50.34 mmol, 2 equiv) and DMF (35 mL) was heated to 120 °C and stirred under N2 atmosphere for 2 
h. The reaction mixture was cooled to 23 °C and poured into ice/water (150 mL). The resulted white
precipitates in the solution were filtered and collected. Then the precipitates were recrystallized from 
minimum acetone to afford the title compound as a white solid (7.53 g, 78%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) 
δ 7.48–7.31 (m, 5 H, PhH), 7.28 (br, 1 H, PhH), 7.22 (br, 1 H, PhH), 6.74 (t, 1 H, PhH), 5.08 (s, 2 H, 
