3.2 Synthesis of Dodecane-Based IAJDs with 3,5-Nonsymmetric Alkyl Chains 
Scheme S2. Synthesis of Dodecane-Based IAJDs with 3,5-Nonsymmetric Alkyl Chains
Reagents and conditions: (i) RBr/ROTs, K2CO3, DMF, 120 °C, 2 h; (ii) H2, Pd/C, DCM, MeOH, 12 h; 
(iii) LiAlH4, THF, 0–23 °C, 1 h; (iv) DCC, DPTS, DCM, 12 h; (v) K2CO3, MeCN, 95 °C, 3 h.
Methyl 3-(benzyloxy)-5-(dodecyloxy)benzoate (9). A mixture of compound 2 (5.50 g, 21.30 mmol, 1 
equiv), 1-bromododecane (5.84 g, 23.43 mmol, 1.1 equiv), K2CO3 (5.89 g, 42.60 mmol, 2 equiv) and 
DMF (20 mL) was heated to 120 °C and stirred under N2 atmosphere for 2 h. The reaction mixture was 
cooled to 23 °C and poured into ice/water (150 mL). The resulted white precipitates in the solution were 
filtered and collected. Then the precipitates were recrystallized from minimum acetone to afford the title 
compound as a white solid (6.53 g, 74%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.49–7.31 (m, 5 H, PhH), 7.27
(br, 1 H, PhH), 7.20 (br, 1 H, PhH), 6.73 (t, 1 H, PhH), 5.08 (s, 2 H, PhCH2O-), 3.97 (t, 2 H, PhOCH2-), 
3.90 (s, 3 H, PhCOOCH3), 1.78 (m, 2 H, PhOCH2CH2CH2(CH2)8CH3), 1.44 (m, 2 H, 
PhOCH2CH2CH2(CH2)8CH3), 1.29 (m, 16 H, PhOCH2CH2CH2(CH2)8CH3), 0.89 (t, 3 H, PhO(CH2)11CH3). 
13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3) δ 167.0, 160.4, 159.9, 136.7, 132.1, 128.8, 128.2, 127.7, 108.3, 108.0, 107.1, 
77.4, 70.4, 68.5, 52.3, 32.1, 29.8, 29.8, 29.7, 29.7, 29.6, 29.5, 29.3, 26.1, 22.8, 14.3. Mp = 36 °C.
