Methyl 3-hydroxy-5-(dodecyloxy)benzoate (10). Compound 9 (6.53 g, 15.8 mmol) was dissolved in a 
mixture of DCM (40 mL) and methanol (20 mL). Then Pd/C (0.34 g, 5 wt%) was added to the solution 
and the flask was evacuated and filled with hydrogen for three times. Afterwards, the mixture was stirred 
at 23 °C under hydrogen atmosphere for 12 h. The reaction mixture was filtered through Celite, and the 
filter cake was washed with DCM. Evaporation of the solvent yielded the title compound as a white solid 
(5.04 g, 95%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.15 (d, 2 H, PhH), 6.62 (t, 1 H, PhH), 5.99 (s, 1 H, PhOH), 
3.95 (t, 2 H, PhOCH2-), 3.90 (s, 3 H, PhCOOCH3), 1.74 (m, 2 H, PhOCH2CH2CH2(CH2)8CH3), 1.43 (m, 
2 H, PhOCH2CH2CH2(CH2)8CH3), 1.27 (m, 16 H, PhOCH2CH2CH2(CH2)8CH3), 0.88 (t, 3 H,
PhO(CH2)11CH3). 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3) δ 167.4, 160.6, 157.0, 157.0, 132.0, 109.2, 107.9, 107.3, 
68.5, 52.5, 34.2, 33.0, 32.1, 29.8, 29.8, 29.7, 29.7, 29.7, 29.6, 29.5, 29.5, 29.3, 28.9, 28.3, 26.1, 22.8, 14.2. 
Mp = 89 °C.
Methyl 3-((2-ethylhexyl)oxy)-5-(dodecyloxy)benzoate (11a). A mixture of compound 10 (0.60 g, 1.78 
mmol, 1 equiv), 2-ethylhexyl bromide (0.38 g, 1.96 mmol, 1.1 equiv), K2CO3 (0.49 g, 3.56 mmol, 2 equiv) 
and DMF (15 mL) was heated to 80 °C and stirred under N2 atmosphere for 12 h. The reaction mixture 
was cooled to 23 °C and DMF was removed under reduced pressure. Then water (20 mL) was added, and 
the resulted mixture was extracted with DCM (20 mL) for three times. The organic phases were collected 
and dried over anhydrous MgSO4. After filtration, the obtained filtrate was concentrated to around 3 mL 
and purified by column chromatography (SiO2) with hexane/EtOAc = 20/1 as the eluent to give the title 
compound as a light-yellow oil (0.55 g, 69%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.16 (br, 2 H, PhH), 6.62 (t, 
1 H, PhH), 3.97 (t, 2 H, PhOCH2(CH2)13CH3), 3.89 (s, 3 H, PhCOOCH3), 3.85 (m, 2 H,
PhOCH2CH(CH2CH3)-), 1.86–1.65 (m, 3 H, PhOCH2CH2(CH2)9CH3 and 
PhOCH2CH(CH2CH3)(CH2)3CH3), 1.57–1.18 (m, 26 H, PhOCH2CH2(CH2)9CH3 and 
PhOCH2CH(CH2CH3)(CH2)3CH3), 1.00–0.82 (m, 9 H, PhO(CH2)11CH3 and 
PhOCH2CH(CH2CH3)(CH2)3CH3). 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3) δ 167.3, 160.6, 160.3, 132.2, 131.9, 
107.9, 107.8, 107.6, 106.7, 70.9, 68.5, 52.4, 52.3, 30.7, 29.8, 29.8, 29.7, 29.7, 29.5, 29.3, 29.2, 26.2, 22.8, 
14.2, 14.2, 11.2.
