Methyl 3-((2-ethylhexyl)oxy)-5-(octadecyloxy)benzoate (35a). A mixture of compound 34 (0.60 g, 1.43 
mmol, 1 equiv), 2-ethylhexyl bromide (0.30 g, 1.57 mmol, 1.1 equiv), K2CO3 (0.39 g, 2.86 mmol, 2 equiv) 
and DMF (15 mL) was heated to 80 °C and stirred under N2 atmosphere for 12 h. The reaction mixture 
was cooled to 23 °C and DMF was removed under reduced pressure. Then water (20 mL) was added, and 
the resulted mixture was extracted with DCM (20 mL) for three times. The organic phases were collected 
and dried over anhydrous MgSO4. After filtration, the obtained filtrate was concentrated to around 3 mL 
and purified by column chromatography (SiO2) with hexane/EtOAc = 20/1 as the eluent to give the title 
compound as a light-yellow oil (0.63 g, 83%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.16 (br, 2 H, PhH), 6.64 (t, 
1 H, PhH), 3.97 (t, 2 H, PhOCH2(CH2)16CH3), 3.90 (s, 3 H, PhCOOCH3), 3.86 (m, 2 H,
PhOCH2CH(CH2CH3)-), 1.85–1.69 (m, 3 H, PhOCH2CH2(CH2)15CH3 and 
PhOCH2CH(CH2CH3)(CH2)3CH3), 1.52–1.17 (m, 38 H, PhOCH2CH2(CH2)15CH3 and 
PhOCH2CH(CH2CH3)(CH2)3CH3), 0.90 (m, 9 H, PhO(CH2)17CH3 and PhOCH2CH(CH2CH3)(CH2)3CH3). 
