Compound 39a was synthesized according to a literature procedure reported by our laboratory.[5] A 
mixture of compound 39a (0.20 g, 0.36 mmol, 1.0 equiv), 1-methylpiperazine (40 mg, 0.40 mmol, 1.1 
equiv), K2CO3 (59 mg, 0.43 mmol, 1.2 equiv) and MeCN (10 mL) was heated to 95 °C and stirred for 3 
h. The reaction mixture was cooled to 23 °C and MeCN was removed under reduced pressure. Then water 
(20 mL) was added, and the resulted mixture was extracted with DCM (20 mL) for three times. The 
organic phases were collected and dried over anhydrous MgSO4. After filtration, the obtained filtrate was 
concentrated to around 3 mL and purified by column chromatography (SiO2) with DCM/MeOH = 30/1
and 15/1 as the eluent. Then the obtained product was dissolved in DCM (20 mL), which was washed by 
NaHCO3 solution (2%, 20 mL). The aqueous phase was extracted by DCM (20 mL) for another two times. 
The organic phases were combined and dried over anhydrous MgSO4. Filtration and evaporation of the 
solvent yielded the title compound as a colorless oil (0.18 g, 83%). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 6.45
(br, 2 H, PhH), 6.38 (t, 1 H, PhH), 5.01 (s, 2 H, PhCH2-), 3.90 (t, 4 H, PhOCH2-), 2.64–2.17 (m, 15 H, -
N(CH2CH2)2N-, -NCH2CH2CH2COO- and -NCH3), 1.83 (m, 2 H, -OCOCH2CH2CH2-), 1.75 (m, 4 H, 
PhOCH2CH2-), 1.44 (m, 4 H, PhOCH2CH2CH2-), 1.27 (br, 22 H, PhOCH2CH2CH2(CH2)4CH3 and 
PhOCH2CH2CH2(CH2)7CH3), 0.87 (t, 6 H, -CH2CH2CH3). 13C NMR (101 MHz, CDCl3) δ 173.3, 160.4, 
138.1, 106.3, 100.8, 68.0, 66.1, 57.6, 55.2, 53.1, 46.0, 32.2, 31.9, 31.8, 29.6, 29.6, 29.4, 29.3, 29.3, 29.2, 
26.0, 22.7, 22.6, 22.2, 14.1, 14.1. Purity by HPLC: 99+%. MALDI-TOF MS m/z of [M + H]+ calculated 
for C35H63N2O4: 575.5; Found: 576.9.
